<script>
   reset_map_controllers();
   document.getElementById("page_status").innerHTML = '';
   document.body.classList.remove('loading');
   document.title = <%= raw(@site_title) %>
   document.getElementById('logo').innerHTML = <%= raw(@site_title) %>
   <% if @current_country=='VK' %>
     document.getElementById('VK').style = "display:inline" 
     document.getElementById('ZL').style = "display:none" 
  <% else %>
     document.getElementById('VK').style = "display:none" 
     document.getElementById('ZL').style = "display:inline" 
  <% end %>
</script>

<div id="actionbar" class="span7">
   <div id="crumbs">
     <%=link_to "Home", '/', remote: true,  :id => 'home', :onclick => "linkHandler('home')" %>
     &nbsp;--&gt;&nbsp;
     <b>Moving from PnP</b>
   </div>
   <div id="controls">
     <% if write_access?  %>
       <%=  link_to "Add Spot", "/posts/new?topic_id="+SPOT_TOPIC.to_s, class: "btn btn-small btn-primary",remote: true, id: "add",   :onclick => "linkHandler('add')"%>
       <%=  link_to "Add Alert", "/posts/new?topic_id="+ALERT_TOPIC.to_s, class: "btn btn-small btn-primary",remote: true, id: "add",   :onclick => "linkHandler('add')"%>
     <% end %>
     <%=render 'map_controls'%>
   </div>
</div>

<div id="right_scroll">
  <%= render 'flash' %>
  <div style="background-image: url(<%=@site_title_image%>); background-size: cover;padding-bottom: 10px; margin-top: -2px;">
    <h1> <%= raw(@site_title_unquoted) %> </h1>
  </div>

  <h2>Migrating accounts from the old parksnpeaks.org server</h2>
  <div class="erow">
    <p><b>Welcome to ontheair</b></p>
    <p>After many years the old parksnpeaks.org site has reached and of life, and the services formerly provided there
     are being migrated to ontheair.   All user accounts have been copied over, but if you want to send spots or alerts
     from the new website then you will need to set up a new password on the new server.</p>

     <p>You have two options:</p>
     <ul>
       <li>If you have access to the email address you use to register with parksnpeaks.org, then click the <b>Password Reset</b> button below. </li>
     
       <li>If you cannot access that email account, you will need to register a new account here using the <b>Create Account</b> button below.</li>
     </ul>
     <p>If neither of these options work for you, then get in touch with me, mattbriggs@yahoo.com and I'll help get things working for you.</p>
   </div>
   <div class="erow">
     <%=  link_to "Password Reset", new_password_reset_path, class: "btn btn-small btn-primary", remote: true, :onclick => "linkHandler('forgot')" %>
     <%=  link_to "Create Account", "/users/new", class: "btn btn-small btn-primary", remote: true, :onclick => "linkHandler('new')" %>
   </div>
    <div class="erow">
      <div class="hrline">
         <hr noshade size="4">
      </div>
    </div>

   <div class="erow">
    <p>Once you have access to your account, then please note the following:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>To use SMS spotting, or to send spots to SOTAwatch, you will need to register your mobile phone number against your account</li>
      <li>Existing iPnP or VKPortalog users will be able to continue to use their existing parksnpeaks APIKey from 
          that app. But for new users or devices, please enter the PIN (from your user profile on this site) in the 
          app for authentication</li>
      <li>You can subscribe to our email lists for spots and alerts on the profile page.  But be aware that emails 
          can be subject to 
          several minutes of delays an that the bulk-email process does not permit filtering by spot type. If you 
          want guaranteed instant notification of spots, as well as more advanced filtering rules on what spots you 
          see, then take a look at the pushover app for your mobile device.  Instructions for setting up pushover 
          with ontheair are in the user's guide.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Full details of how to use ontheair are in the <b>Users Guide</b>, which can be found in the <b>Info</b> menu. 
       This guide was originally written wth ZL operators in mind, so sorry for that. We hope to make if  more 
       VK-focussed in future</p>
   </div>

 
     
</div>
<script>
document.getElementById('actionbar-full').innerHTML=document.getElementById('actionbar').innerHTML;
if ($(window).width() < 960) {
        site_smaller_map();
      }

</script>

